  "caveats": [
    "Primary statewide turnout coverage uses official EAC 2024 EAVS V2 jurisdiction-level fallback data because the WEC ward-by-ward federal/state results workbook does not include registered-voter denominator fields.",
    "EAC F1a Total Voters is not the same measure as WEC presidential contest total votes, so it should not be reconciled against the presidential total as if they were identical.",
    "Two EAC Wisconsin jurisdiction rows have zero registered voters; those normalized turnout percentages are blank and warning-gated.",
    "Dane currently contributes one county-level row, not ward-level denominator rows.",
    "Milwaukee and Oneida denominators are pre-Election-Day or explicitly dated before Election Day.",
    "Jefferson denominator timing is unknown.",
    "Wisconsin allows Election Day registration, so pre-Election-Day denominators can understate final registration and inflate apparent turnout rates.",
    "Local partial rows remain useful supplemental provenance but are not the primary statewide turnout dataset.",
    "Prefer WEC/county ward-level denominator artifacts if a statewide official Wisconsin denominator file becomes available."
  ]
